# Multi-electron term symbols (crystod-group --multiplet); testsuite section 14
# Spin multiplicities 2S+1, sorted by descending multiplicity (Hund ground term first).
# Shell tokens: T2g2 = T2g^2 (the ^-free form needs no quoting in zsh).
# With --orbital, exact Coulomb multiplet energies (Racah A, B, C for d shells;
# reduced Slater-Condon F0/F2/F4/F6 for f shells) and the ground state are printed.

$ crystod-group --multiplet T2g3 --pg m-3m --orbital d

* Point group *
m-3m

* Ligand-field splitting of the d orbital *
1(Eg) + 1(T2g)

* Configuration *
(T2g)^3

* Term Symbols *
(T2g)^3 = ^4A2g + ^2Eg + ^2T1g + ^2T2g

check: 20 states = C(6,3) = 20

* Multiplet Energies (Racah parameters A, B, C; Coulomb part only) *
^4A2g: 3A - 15B
^2Eg : 3A - 6B + 3C
^2T1g: 3A - 6B + 3C
^2T2g: 3A + 5C
(the one-electron / crystal-field part is an additive constant within the configuration)

* Ground-state Term Symbol (within this configuration) *
^4A2g   (lowest for any B > 0, C > 0)


