$ crystod-group --multiplet T2g2 Eg1 --pg m-3m --orbital d

* Point group *
m-3m

* Ligand-field splitting of the d orbital *
1(Eg) + 1(T2g)

* Configuration *
(T2g)^2 (Eg)^1

* Term Symbols *
(T2g)^2 (Eg)^1 = ^4T1g + ^4T2g + ^2A1g + ^2A2g + 2(^2Eg) + 2(^2T1g) + 2(^2T2g)

check: 60 states = C(6,2) x C(4,1) = 60

* Multiplet Energies (Racah parameters A, B, C; Coulomb part only) *
^4T1g: 3A - 3B
^4T2g: 3A - 15B
^2A1g: 3A - 11B + 3C
^2A2g: 3A + 9B + 3C
^2Eg : 3A + (7/2)B + (9/2)C +- (1/2)sqrt(481B^2 + 54BC + 9C^2)   (x2, configuration mixing)
^2T1g: 3A - 3B + 3C +- 3sqrt(2)B   (x2, configuration mixing)
^2T2g: 3A - B + 3C +- sqrt(34)B   (x2, configuration mixing)
(numeric CI blocks evaluated at C/B = 4.5, typical for 3d ions)
(the one-electron / crystal-field part is an additive constant within the configuration)

* Ground-state Term Symbol (within this configuration) *
^4T2g   (lowest at C/B = 4.5, typical for 3d ions)


